<document
    `{ author: "anonymous@elsewhere" }
    <stack
        <heading `{level: 2} "A message from a stranger">

        <text "This document arrived over the wire from someone you do not trust.
               It carries programs in several languages. A bassline renderer can
               display all of it safely, running only what it chooses — because the
               grammar itself marks instruction apart from content.">

        <block `{language: "forth"} "6 7 *">
        <block `{language: "python"} "import os; os.system('wipe-everything')">
        <block `{language: "sql"} "DROP TABLE users;">

        <text "The forth block offers to run, because this renderer speaks forth.
               The python and sql blocks are held inert — present, inspectable,
               never executed. Nothing ran on load. Compare an HTML document, where
               a script tag executes the moment the page is parsed.">
    >
>
